{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
There's a [G]dark and a troubled side of [C]life;
There's a [G]bright and a sunny side [D7]too;
Tho' we [G]meet with the darkness and [C]strife,
The [G]sunny side [D7]we also may [G]view.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
Keep on the [G]sunny side,
Always on the [C]sunny [G]side,
Keep on the sunny side of [D7]life;
It will [G]help us every day,
It will [C]brighten all the [G]way,
If we'll [G]keep on the [D7]sunny side of [G]life.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
Tho' the [G]storm in its fury break to[C]day,
Crushing [G]hopes that we cherished so [D7]dear,
Storm and [G]cloud will in time pass a[C]way,
The [G]sun again [D7]will shine bright and [G]clear.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 3"}
Let us [G]greet with a song of hope each [C]day,
Tho' the [G]moment be cloudy or [D7]fair;
Let us [G]trust in our Saviour al[C]way,
Who [G]keepeth [D7]everyone in His [G]care.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
{x_end: G}
